  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "P4119-A",
      "skill": "engineering-abstract-contributions",
      "language": "en+zh",
      "prompt": "A. 请根据以下完全虚构、已确认的研究说明，写一版自然连贯的英文摘要（约180-210词，不必凑字数），再给出适当数量的英文贡献点。不要编号列举摘要中的模块，也不要添加尚未提供的事实。研究对象为连续化学混合过程的产品浓度预测；传感器采样间隔不同，浓度化验标签稀疏。参考方案将测量前向填充到统一时间网格，再进行监督预测。本文模型直接把每个窗口内已获得的测量值、变量标识及其距预测时刻的时间间隔编码为观测表征，只使用预测时刻之前的测量。一个加权读出将这些观测表征组合为窗口表征，质量预测头据此估计浓度。在训练中，人工遮去部分原本已观测的数值，由辅助解码器重构这些值；重构目标用有标签和无标签训练窗口，质量损失只用有标签窗口。这两个目标训练共同编码器，预测时不执行辅助解码器，也不先重建完整时间网格。已完成的相关文献比较支持将‘按实际观测时间编码与联合质量学习的结合’作为本研究的具体推进点；没有全领域首创依据，标准编码器不单独算创新。虚构实验在一个过程模拟案例和一个实际生产数据案例上完成，采用独立留出的生产时段，不接触测试标签调参。结果在测试的原生采样设置下比前向填充监督参考方案具有更低浓度预测误差；删去时间间隔编码或无标签重构目标都使预测误差增加。没有部署、闭环控制、跨工厂迁移、运行速度或普适信息恢复证据，不给数值。请让读者能读出操作之间为何相连，以及实验回答了什么问题。必要的作者说明与摘要正文分开。",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Carry asynchronous measurements to an observation representation, shared training objectives and the retained predictor without a fictional imputation pipeline.",
        "Keep readout separate from quality supervision and training-only decoder; no future measurements or test-label access.",
        "Explain the engineering requirement and integration advance using connected prose, not a sequence of module announcements.",
        "End with the supplied bounded comparison and case provenance; do not repeat a list of unavailable evidence in the abstract.",
        "Keep contribution count and novelty bounded to the supplied integration; no independent novelty for standard encoder or routine case studies."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Invent online adaptation, causal graph, recovery of all missing values, deployment or generalization beyond the stated population.",
        "Treat reconstruction as a required test-time step or imply it produces the quality target.",
        "Copy source-paper wording or import private manuscript facts."
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "One integration contribution with ablation support; positive retained predictor and scoped evidence.",
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
        "engineering-abstract-contributions-zh"
      ],
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic and organization review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4119-revised.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4119-independent-evaluation.md",
      "evaluation_phase": "fresh_context_after_targeted_repair"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4119-B",
      "skill": "engineering-abstract-contributions",
      "language": "en+zh",
      "prompt": "B. 另一项完全虚构的研究针对过程故障零样本诊断。只有已见故障类别有训练样本；工程师预先为已见及候选未见类别定义同一组语义属性，如温度上升、压力下降，这些是故障描述而不是传感器变量本身。编码器及属性预测头用已见类别样本训练。另留出的已见类别验证样本用于估计各属性的预测误差，据此得到固定的属性权重，误差较小的属性具有较大权重。预测时输出属性向量，再用这些固定权重计算该向量与预先给定候选未见类别描述的加权距离，选择距离最小的类别。没有未知类别拒识、测试时更新或校准不确定度输出。相近文献已支持‘预测属性后匹配类别描述’这一路线；本研究具体改动是让已见类别验证误差决定匹配中各属性的权重，不声称发明整个零样本诊断范式。一个虚构真实生产数据案例中，按类别留出未见故障，所有未见类别样本只在最终测试使用。给定比较结果为：与同一属性预测器的等权距离相比，加权距离在该留出类别集合上提高诊断准确率；没有给出其他结果或具体数值。请写英文摘要（接近180-200词即可，清楚比长度重要）及适当数量的贡献点，强调工程需求、所改动的操作以及它如何通向故障类别判断。保留attribute的语义，不把它统一换成variable；避免空泛优越性、自我防御和模块清单。不要在正文里列出所有未开展的研究，确有必要的作者提醒另放。",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Keep semantic attributes distinct from measured variables and distinguish known candidate unseen classes from open-set unknown rejection.",
        "Link held-out seen-class attribute errors to fixed weighting and weighted semantic matching, not a test-time adaptive gate or calibrated uncertainty.",
        "Keep the established encoder/predictor route as context and the weighting change as the bounded contribution.",
        "Write an informative bounded result and connected prose without a repeated defensive tail."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Infer that low seen-class attribute error proves reliability or optimality on every unseen class.",
        "Invent unseen-class training data, pseudo-label training, fuzzy inference, online parameter updates or industrial deployment.",
        "Inflate routine evaluation or standard zero-shot attribute prediction into separate novelty claims."
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "Semantic attributes and fixed seen-validation weighting preserved; held-out class result bounded.",
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
        "engineering-abstract-contributions-zh"
      ],
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic and organization review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4119-revised.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4119-independent-evaluation.md",
      "evaluation_phase": "fresh_context_after_targeted_repair"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4119-C",
      "skill": "engineering-abstract-contributions",
      "language": "en+zh",
      "prompt": "C. 以下也是虚构事实。一项过程质量预测研究没有提出新神经网络，其主要问题是：在相同传感器采集预算下，采样时刻的分配是否会改变扰动后的预测质量？研究在预先规定的两种采样安排下，固定数据来源、预测器、训练信息和总观测数，并在独立留出的生产时段比较。观察到常规时段的平均误差相近，但把采样机会分配到扰动后的安排，在所测扰动窗口具有较低的预测峰值误差。研究已对这一预先提出的问题完成相应重复比较；没有声称新算法、普适最优采样或闭环收益。请判断这能否写成一项实证贡献，并给出一条可用的英文贡献表述及简短中文理由。不要只因没有新模块就删掉其贡献，也不要编数值或扩大结果范围。",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Recognize a distinct empirical question about sampling placement under equal budgets, not merely validation of a proposed model.",
        "State the actual ordinary-period versus disturbance-window finding with held-out scope and no invented architecture.",
        "Preserve the legitimate empirical contribution while avoiding causal or universal optimality claims beyond the specified comparison."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Reject every empirical contribution because no new network exists.",
        "Rewrite the study as a novel adaptive controller or deployed optimization result."
      ],
      "evidence_type": "fresh-context fictional author request; positive control added after baseline",
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "Legitimate independent empirical question retained without invented new architecture or universal optimality.",
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
        "engineering-abstract-contributions-zh"
      ],
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic and organization review; no independent second grader",
